# ATLAS

## Commercial Fees & Payment Schedule

**Document Type:** Commercial Pricing & Payment Schedule
**Applicable To:** Atlas Admissions Platform
**Currency:** South African Rand (ZAR)
**Version:** 1.0

---

## 1. Purpose

This Commercial Fees & Payment Schedule sets out the fees payable by the Institution for the implementation, licensing, support and usage of the Atlas Admissions Platform.

The purpose of this document is to provide a clear and transparent description of the commercial charges applicable to the Institution and to distinguish Atlas charges from third-party infrastructure costs.

This document is intended to form part of the commercial agreement between **Atlas** and the **Institution** and should be read together with the applicable Atlas service agreement, terms and conditions, and any agreed implementation or service documentation.

---

# 2. Atlas Commercial Fee Structure

The Institution's Atlas charges consist of the following:

| Fee                                        |                                   Amount | Frequency                        |
| ------------------------------------------ | ---------------------------------------: | -------------------------------- |
| Implementation, Customisation & Deployment |                              **R20,000** | Once-off                         |
| Annual Atlas Licence & Support             |                              **R30,000** | Annual, paid upfront             |
| Atlas Application Charge                   | **R7 per successfully paid application** | Annual, billed in arrears        |
| Firebase / Google Cloud Infrastructure     |         **Paid directly by Institution** | According to third-party billing |

All amounts stated in this document are in **South African Rand (ZAR)**.

Unless otherwise stated in a signed agreement, applicable taxes, including VAT where legally applicable, are additional.

---

# 3. Implementation, Customisation & Deployment Fee

## 3.1 Fee

**R20,000 once-off**

The Implementation, Customisation & Deployment Fee is payable once when the Institution initially adopts and deploys Atlas.

## 3.2 Purpose

This fee covers the initial professional services required to prepare Atlas for operational use by the Institution.

The implementation process may include:

* Initial Atlas environment configuration
* Institution branding and identity configuration
* Application process configuration
* Application field configuration
* Programme and course configuration
* Campus configuration
* Application-cycle configuration
* Applicant-facing configuration
* Staff and administrative access configuration
* Role configuration
* Initial workflow configuration
* Payment configuration
* Initial testing and verification
* Deployment and production launch
* Initial implementation support

The specific configuration and customisation delivered to the Institution will be determined during the implementation process and may be documented in an agreed implementation specification.

## 3.3 Payment

The Implementation, Customisation & Deployment Fee is payable in accordance with the agreed implementation commencement terms.

Atlas will commence implementation and deployment activities subject to the applicable commercial and contractual requirements being satisfied.

## 3.4 Once-Off Nature

The Implementation, Customisation & Deployment Fee is a once-off charge for the Institution's initial Atlas implementation.

It does not constitute an annual fee.

Additional implementation work, major customisation projects, integrations or services outside the agreed implementation scope may be quoted separately where applicable.

---

# 4. Annual Atlas Licence & Support Fee

## 4.1 Fee

**R30,000 per year**

The Annual Atlas Licence & Support Fee provides the Institution with continued access to and use of the Atlas software platform during the applicable licence period, together with the ongoing software maintenance and support services included within the Atlas service offering.

## 4.2 The Annual Licence Includes

Subject to the applicable Atlas service agreement, the Annual Atlas Licence & Support Fee covers:

* Continued licence to use Atlas
* Continued access to the Atlas Admissions Platform
* Ongoing software maintenance
* Corrective maintenance and bug fixes
* Software updates
* Security-related software maintenance
* Ongoing technical support
* Assistance with normal Atlas platform operation
* Support for authorised Institution users
* Ongoing maintenance of the Atlas software platform
* Continued access to applicable Atlas features included within the Institution's licensed service

## 4.3 Licence Period

The standard Atlas annual licence period operates on a yearly basis.

For Institutions commencing Atlas during an existing calendar year, the first-year licence charge may be adjusted in accordance with the agreed commencement date and commercial terms.

Thereafter, the Annual Atlas Licence & Support Fee is payable annually in advance in accordance with the applicable renewal date.

## 4.4 What the Annual Licence Does Not Include

The Annual Atlas Licence & Support Fee does not include the Institution's third-party infrastructure charges, including Firebase or Google Cloud charges.

The Institution remains responsible for maintaining and paying for its required third-party infrastructure directly.

