# 6. Firebase / Google Cloud Infrastructure

## 6.1 Third-Party Infrastructure

Firebase and/or Google Cloud infrastructure used in connection with the Institution's Atlas deployment is **not included in the Atlas fees**.

The Institution is responsible for its applicable Firebase / Google Cloud account and associated infrastructure costs.

## 6.2 Direct Billing

Where the Atlas deployment uses Firebase and/or Google Cloud services, the applicable infrastructure charges are billed directly to the Institution by the relevant third-party service provider.

Atlas does not include these infrastructure charges within the Annual Atlas Licence & Support Fee or Atlas Application Charge.

## 6.3 Examples of Third-Party Infrastructure Costs

Depending on the Institution's technical configuration and usage, third-party infrastructure charges may include:

* Database usage
* Cloud storage
* Data transfer
* Cloud Functions or other compute services
* Authentication services
* Other applicable Firebase services
* Other applicable Google Cloud services

Actual third-party infrastructure charges are determined by the applicable provider and the Institution's usage.

---

# 7. Annual Billing Cycle

The standard Atlas annual application period operates from **1 January to 30 November**.

The standard commercial cycle is as follows:

| Date / Period           | Payment / Event                                                                                     |
| ----------------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |
| Initial go-live         | **R20,000** Implementation, Customisation & Deployment Fee                                          |
| 1 January – 30 November | Annual Atlas Licence period and application activity                                                |
| 1 January               | **R30,000** Annual Atlas Licence & Support Fee for the new licence year                             |
| 1 January – 30 November | Successfully paid applications accumulate for application billing                                   |
| 30 November             | Annual application-volume period closes                                                             |
| 1–30 December           | Atlas calculates the Application Charge based on the final number of successfully paid applications |
| 1–30 December           | Institution pays the Application Charge for the completed application period                        |
| Following 1 January     | New annual licence period begins                                                                    |

For an Institution commencing Atlas after 1 January, the first licence period and application period will be handled according to the agreed commencement date and applicable implementation terms.

---

# 8. Payment Responsibility

The Institution is responsible for payment of:

1. The Implementation, Customisation & Deployment Fee;
2. The Annual Atlas Licence & Support Fee;
3. The Atlas Application Charge; and
4. Any applicable third-party infrastructure costs payable directly to Firebase / Google Cloud.

Atlas fees and third-party infrastructure charges are separate financial obligations.

Payment of Firebase / Google Cloud charges does not satisfy or reduce any amount payable to Atlas.

